<title>UK: BNCE sets $300 million five-year bond, +166 bp.</title>
<headline>BNCE sets $300 million five-year bond, +166 bp.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers BTI and Banco Santander.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANCO NACIONAL DE COMERCIO EXTERIOR</p>
<p> AMT    $300 MLN	COUPON     8.0 PCT   MATURITY    18.JUL.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE    18.JUL.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.375     REOFFER    PAR	 SPREAD	+166 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	BA2	 LISTING    LUX</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  BB	  DENOMS (K) 10	  SALE LIMITS US/UK/MX</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  TAX PROVS  STD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.125     SELL CONC  0.25</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.25 PCT JUNE 2002 UST</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
